      {
        "name": "The Two Worlds Rule",
        "body": "Story pages are always bright, whatever the app theme is set to. Working pages follow the theme. When working components appear inside a story page, they render within a dark product window using the scoped window palette.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Unrated Rule",
        "body": "A company with no rating never takes a series colour. Its bands are drawn with a hatched line-strong pattern and its markers in ink-3.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Means Number Rule",
        "body": "Geist Mono with tabular numerals is used for figures, tickers, ticker inputs, counts, kbd hints and formulas. It is never used for prose. Placeholders inside mono inputs switch back to Geist.",
        "section": "typography"
